<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Sidewalks &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://osm-guelph.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph Sidewalks &mdash; OSM coverage gaps</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count headline"><strong>{{UNTRACED_KM}} km</strong><span>of City sidewalk with no OSM line within {{MATCH_M}}&nbsp;m</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{STREETS}}</strong><span>streets with &ge;&nbsp;{{STREET_MIN_KM}}&nbsp;km of it</span></div>
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>missing</span></div>
    <div class="count partial"><strong>{{PARTIAL_COUNT}}</strong><span>partial</span></div>
    <div class="count far"><strong>{{FAR_COUNT}}</strong><span>far</span></div>
    <div class="count road_says_no"><strong>{{SAYS_NO_COUNT}}</strong><span>road says no</span></div>
    <div class="count untagged"><strong>{{UNTAGGED_COUNT}}</strong><span>untagged footway</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{CITY_KM}} km</strong><span>City sidewalk built</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{OSM_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM sidewalk ways</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City data {{DATA_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <p class="note">
    The City layer is accurate to 1&ndash;5&nbsp;m, and {{FAR_KM}}&nbsp;km of the
    untraced length sits {{MATCH_M}}&ndash;{{FAR_M}}&nbsp;m from an OSM line, so
    the honest figure is ~{{HONEST_LOW_KM}}&ndash;{{HONEST_HIGH_KM}}&nbsp;km;
    {{REMOTE_KM}}&nbsp;km has nothing within {{REMOTE_M}}&nbsp;m. The original
    audit's &ldquo;OSM has 92%&rdquo; divided total lengths &mdash; it never
    asked whether they are the same sidewalks.
  </p>
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Source: <a href="{{DATASET_PAGE}}">Sidewalks</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-geojson="gaps.geojson"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
       data-raster-maxzoom="{{RASTER_MAXZOOM}}"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label title="Under {{PARTIAL_PCT}} traced, no OSM line nearby"><span class="swatch missing"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-missing" checked> Missing</label>
        <label title="{{PARTIAL_PCT}} to {{MATCHED_PCT}} traced"><span class="swatch partial"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-partial" checked> Partial</label>
        <label title="An OSM line {{MATCH_M}}-{{FAR_M}} m away: check the alignment before adding one"><span class="swatch far"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-far" checked> Far</label>
        <label title="The OSM road says sidewalk=no where the City has one"><span class="swatch road_says_no"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-road_says_no" checked> Road says no</label>
        <label title="Covered by a plain highway=footway: tag it footway=sidewalk"><span class="swatch untagged"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-untagged" checked> Untagged</label>
        <label title="Mapped as sidewalk=* on the road: a valid way to map it ({{ON_ROAD_COUNT}} segments)"><span class="swatch on_road_tag"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-on_road_tag"> On road tag</label>
        <label title="City status PROPOSED: may not be poured yet ({{PROPOSED_COUNT}} segments)"><span class="swatch proposed"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-proposed"> Proposed</label>
        <label title="Matched sidewalk way with no surface=* ({{NOSURFACE_COUNT}} segments)"><span class="swatch nosurface"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-nosurface"> No surface</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by street or id...">
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        Each City sidewalk is sampled every {{SAMPLE_STEP_M}}&nbsp;m; a sample
        counts as traced when OSM has a pedestrian line (or a road tagged
        <code>sidewalk=*</code>) within {{MATCH_M}}&nbsp;m, and a segment
        &ge;&nbsp;{{MATCHED_PCT}} traced is matched. Streets are named after
        the nearest OSM road, so their count may differ slightly from the
        audit's 97, which used City centrelines. Click a street to zoom to it
        and list its segments; click a segment (or a line on the map) to select
        it, then press <kbd>O</kbd> to open the spot on openstreetmap.org or
        <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD editor (each segment has the same
        <strong>OSM&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;iD</strong> link pair). Cyan lines from
        z15 are the City's own layer; check current imagery before adding
        anything.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th class="col-name">Street / segment</th><th>Untraced</th>
              <th>Segments</th><th>Links</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
